# Full Local Runtime

Run every implemented Foundry stage and continue through the safe shadow
boundary in one process:

```bash
python -m src.foundry \
  examples/idea_observations/input.jsonl \
  --output-dir receipts/full_run \
  --scenario-count 30 \
  --current-level 2 \
  --next-level 3 \
  --shadow-bindings examples/full_run/adapter_bindings.yaml \
  --execution-inputs examples/full_run/execution_inputs.yaml
```

The execution boundary can also be rerun independently:

```bash
python -m src.execution \
  receipts/full_run/03_protocol_candidates.yaml \
  receipts/full_run/06_poc_promotions.yaml \
  examples/full_run/adapter_bindings.yaml \
  --inputs examples/full_run/execution_inputs.yaml \
  --output-dir receipts/full_run
```

A generated candidate begins as `intent.status: unconfirmed`, so the expected
first Action Receipt is normally `blocked`, not `shadowed`. That is correct: the
runtime has completed the path and proved that an unconfirmed or insufficiently
promoted candidate cannot cross the execution boundary.

A `shadowed` result requires all of the following:

- candidate intent is explicitly `confirmed`;
- promotion decision is `PROMOTE`;
- promotion eligibility and every declared check are true;
- requested next level is at least Level 3;
- blocking conditions are met or waived;
- no approval is pending or rejected;
- required inputs are present;
- every action has an enabled binding.

Shadow mode never invokes adapters and always records `external_effects: []`.

## Immediate READY fixture

The included synthetic fixture proves the final boundary independently of the
upstream generation stages:

```bash
python -m src.execution \
  examples/full_run/shadow_ready_candidates.yaml \
  examples/full_run/shadow_ready_promotions.yaml \
  examples/full_run/adapter_bindings.yaml \
  --inputs examples/full_run/execution_inputs.yaml \
  --output-dir receipts/shadow_ready \
  --require-ready
```

Expected result: one `shadowed` Action Receipt, `READY`, and zero external
effects. The fixture is synthetic validation material, not production evidence.
